- dwp: https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/ns#
'@graph': []
context_profile:
  schema: okf-dwp-context-authoring.v1
  scope: 'Frozen DMG research: listed legacy JSA(Cont), JSA(IB), IS, SPC and ESA(Cont)/ESA(IR) imprisonment
    guidance captured on 15 September 2026. This is an explanation of the captured text, not a determination
    of contemporary individual eligibility.'
  limitations:
  - Independent experimental research, not an official DWP document, benefits advice, a calculation
    or an individual entitlement decision. All authored meanings and dependencies require specialist
    review.
  - The broad labels JSA and ESA do not establish a claimant’s regime. This profile explains the
    listed DMG legacy regimes; New Style JSA/ESA, UC and PIP are routed to ADM by 12016. Those ADM
    bodies are not acquired. Ask for regime/date and fresh authoritative checks before applying
    guidance to a person.
  - The payability statement at 12003 is scoped by the list in 12002. It cannot replace
    benefit-specific rules or establish that entitlement always survives imprisonment.
  - Machine-extracted whole pages retain neighbouring text, partial unrelated paragraphs, footnotes,
    historical examples and possible reading-order errors. Use the stated locators; page presence is
    not full legal interpretation or PDF visual review.
  - Capture date is not publication, revision or commencement. Old amendment footers and example
    dates remain literal source text. The currently linked catalogue is not current-law assurance;
    legislation and case law have not been consolidated or reconciled.
  - The frozen PDFs still refer to Memo 07/20. Official catalogue history says it was removed
    because the regulations ceased to have effect from 31 August 2021. The memo body is absent; do
    not revive that temporary exception.
  - 12016’s ADM M1 reference conflicts with the frozen catalogue title marking M1 spare. S1/U6 are
    identified routes, not acquired evidence. Internal Chapter 41 references to 53112 and 53071 and
    the printed Chapter 53 number 531261 remain unresolved version/typographic observations.
  - 'Prisoner definitions differ by benefit: do not transfer the general criminal/civil distinction indiscriminately.
    Remand, bail hostel, sentence, release, hospital legislation, fine default, overseas detention, time
    limits and partner circumstances require the relevant branch. Housing-cost passages do not establish
    a current housing award.'
  authored_at: '2026-09-16T00:48:43.670101Z'
