- route: term/common-imprisonment-payability
  context_assembly:
    kind: concept
    scope: 'Frozen DMG research: listed legacy JSA(Cont), JSA(IB), IS, SPC and ESA(Cont)/ESA(IR) imprisonment
      guidance captured on 15 September 2026. This is an explanation of the captured text, not a determination
      of contemporary individual eligibility.'
    aliases:
    - imprisoned
    - imprisonment
    - prisoner
    - prisoners
    - custody
    - detained
    - detention in legal custody
    - detained in legal custody
    text: The general 12003 payability statement applies to the benefits listed in 12002; 12015
      separately routes JSA, IS, SPC and the two ESA components to their own chapters. It is not a
      universal claim that custody leaves entitlement intact. Prisoner/custody meanings vary by
      benefit and status. The broad labels JSA and ESA do not establish a claimant’s regime. This
      profile explains the listed DMG legacy regimes; New Style JSA/ESA, UC and PIP are routed to
      ADM by 12016. Those ADM bodies are not acquired. Ask for regime/date and fresh authoritative
      checks before applying guidance to a person.
    relations:
    - target: page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0002
      predicate: http://purl.org/dc/terms/requires
      rationale: The expression these benefits in 12003 requires the start of the 12002 list.
      evidence:
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0002
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
    - target: scope/legacy-imprisonment-guidance
      predicate: http://purl.org/dc/terms/requires
      rationale: All use of the general imprisonment concept needs its regime and authority
        boundary.
      evidence:
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
    - target: term/legacy-jsa-custody-availability
      predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
      rationale: 12015 expressly routes this imprisonment issue to the benefit-specific chapter;
        this is related context, not a shared legal outcome.
      evidence:
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
    - target: term/is-prisoner-applicable-amount
      predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
      rationale: 12015 expressly routes this imprisonment issue to the benefit-specific chapter;
        this is related context, not a shared legal outcome.
      evidence:
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
    - target: term/pc-prisoner-credit-rates
      predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
      rationale: 12015 expressly routes this imprisonment issue to the benefit-specific chapter;
        this is related context, not a shared legal outcome.
      evidence:
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
    - target: term/esa-contributory-custody
      predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
      rationale: 12015 expressly routes this imprisonment issue to the benefit-specific chapter;
        this is related context, not a shared legal outcome.
      evidence:
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
    - target: term/esa-income-related-custody
      predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
      rationale: 12015 expressly routes this imprisonment issue to the benefit-specific chapter;
        this is related context, not a shared legal outcome.
      evidence:
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
    - target: term/benefit-disqualification
      predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
      rationale: The custody guidance discusses disqualification as a separate benefit mechanism,
        not as a synonym for imprisonment.
      evidence:
      - page/dmg-vol3-ch12/0003
      - page/dmg-vol9-ch53/0054
